  "status_text": "A circuit can keep its answers even when some wires go dark and others light up by mistake. Lean checked exactly when a row of parallel NOT gates between two AND/OR stages can do it, with the last stage also reading the raw inputs (L-meta-53185). Assign each sample a rank between zero and the number of NOT gates. Compare inputs that only turn wires on. Ranks must stay level or rise. If a required output turns off, the rank must rise by more than the earlier sample can lose plus the later sample can gain. Two possible losses and one gain then require a rise of at least four.",
